BARRIER-BYTEOFF: barrier-collision tables + car-flag word indexed with byte offsets

FUN_0044520c (Barrier_Collision helper; L8/L10 render-loop crash frame) reads
`*(uint *)(&DAT_00466eac + param_2 * 4)` / `&DAT_00466ebc + param_2 * 4` -- the explicit *4 is a
BYTE stride into two 4-entry int tables @0x466eac/0x466ebc, but the symbols are int*-typed GIMG
macros so the offset scales x4 -> reads 4x too far -> garbage table values -> wild read
0xc0796a20/0xbf396a20 at `iVar2 + 0x792b2e + uVar1 * 4`. Likewise `(&DAT_00792a30)[iVar2]` uses
iVar2 = car*0x1b2, the car-struct BYTE offset (sibling fields use raw `iVar2 + 0x792xxx`), as an
int index -> x4. Byte-address all three. Same Ghidra pointer-scaling class as COLOURMAT-BYTEOFF.

